# Scacelith - हिन्दी (Hindi)
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals: one|other (0 and 1 are "one").
# Register: formal "आप", as in Microsoft and Apple Hindi software. Buttons and commands use the polite
# imperative in -ें / -एँ (चुनें, सहेजें, रद्द करें, हार मानें). Hindi has no capitals: titles are plain text.
# The player's gender is unknown, and a Hindi verb agrees with its subject (also with "आप"). With the
# player as the subject the lines use only the imperative, the subjunctive, the present copula "हैं",
# ने with a transitive perfective (आपने बाज़ी छोड़ दी), dative subjects (आपको ... मिलेगा), nouns
# (आपकी जीत हुई, आपके मोहरे सफ़ेद होंगे) or the passive (बदला जा सकता है); never "आप जीत गए",
# "आप खेलेंगे", "आप कर सकते हैं", "पासवर्ड भूल गए?". Other people named by {0} get the same care.
# Terms: see the Hindi glossary (बाज़ी, चाल, शह, मात, स्टेलमेट, ड्रॉ, हार मानें, टाइम कंट्रोल, स्कोरशीट...).
# Named keys keep the names printed on Indian (English) keyboards: Space, Shift, Ctrl, Backspace, Home / End.

